"107:003 106:3 and gathered them out of the countries, from the east, and west, and north, and south.",
"107:004 106:4 They wandered in the wilderness in a dry land; they found no way to a city of habitation.",
"107:005 106:5 Hungry and thirsty, their soul fainted in them.",
"107:006 106:6 Then they cried to the Lord in their affliction, and he delivered them out of their distresses.",
"107:007 106:7 And he guided them into a straight path, that they might go to a city of habitation.",
"107:008 106:8 Let them acknowledge to the Lord his mercies, and his wonderful works to the children of men.",
"107:009 106:9 For he satisfies the empty soul, and fills the hungry soul with good things,",
"107:010 106:10 even them that sit in darkness and the shadow of death, fettered in poverty and iron;",
"107:011 106:11 because they rebelled against the words of God, and provoked the counsel of the Most High.",
"107:012 106:12 So their heart was brought low with troubles; they were weak, and there was no helper.",
"107:013 106:13 Then they cried to the Lord in their affliction, and he saved them out of their distresses.",
"107:014 106:14 And he brought them out of darkness and the shadow of death, and broke their bonds asunder.",
"107:015 106:15 Let them acknowledge to the Lord his mercies, and his wonders to the children of men.",
"107:016 106:16 For he broke to pieces the brazen gates, and crushed the iron bars.",
"107:017 106:17 He helped them out of the way of their iniquity; for they were brought low because of their iniquities.",
"107:018 106:18 Their soul abhorred all meat; and they drew near to the gates of death.",
"107:019 106:19 Then they cried to the Lord in their affliction, and he saved them out of their distresses.",
"107:020 106:20 He sent his word, and healed them, and delivered them out of their destructions.",
"107:021 106:21 Let them acknowledge to the Lord his mercies, and his wonderful works to the children of men.",
"107:022 106:22 And let them offer to him the sacrifice of praise, and proclaim this works with exultation.",
"107:023 106:23 They that go down to the sea in ships, doing business in many waters;",
"107:024 106:24 these men have seen the works of the Lord, and his wonders in the deep.",
"107:025 106:25 He speaks, and the stormy wind arises, and its waves are lifted up.",
"107:026 106:26 They go up to the heavens, and go down to the depths; their soul melts because of troubles.",
"107:027 106:27 They are troubled, they stagger as a drunkard, and all their wisdom is swallowed up.",
"107:028 106:28 Then they cry to the Lord in their affliction, and he brings them out of their distresses.",
"107:029 106:29 And he commands the storm, and it is calmed into a gentle breeze, and its waves are still.",
